  "dn24:1.4.14": "See detailed discussion of this idiom in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn12/en/sujato#2.5'>MN 12:2.5</a>. Here the form varies somewhat. The pronoun (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>mayā</i>) in instrumental explicitly qualifies “Dhamma taught <em>by me</em>”. Elsewhere the pronoun in genitive qualifies <i lang='pi' translate='no'>atthāya</i>, “the goal <em>for him</em>”. ",
