  "dn24:1.9.5": "This whole passage is unprecedented in early Buddhism. If Sunakkhatta was indeed able to revive the dead with three punches, it would explain why he thought so little of the Buddha’s powers. But the ease with which this information is obtained contrasts with the elaborate failures of Pāyāsi (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn23/en/sujato'>DN 23</a>). ",
